0..60 Comment "//! `ring-base` defines the mock ring protocols and entries."
61..64 Comment "//!"
65..137 Comment "//! Each submission owes one completion. The pathological twins refuse a"
138..208 Comment "//! completion left pending and a buffer reused before its completion."
209..212 Comment "//!"
213..292 Comment "//! The checker gives the submitter a pending completion after it sends `read`."
293..365 Comment "//! The imported declarations give every completion source one protocol."
366..369 Comment "//!"
370..433 Comment "//! - see: corpus/pathological/completion/pending-dropped.gandr"
434..496 Comment "//! - see: corpus/pathological/completion/buffer-touched.gandr"
497..544 Comment "//! - see: https://without.boats/blog/io-uring/"
546..618 Comment "/// A ring: its entries sealed behind the interface, the protocol of one"
619..696 Comment "/// submission as the kernel serves it, the buffer and the pending completion"
697..769 Comment "/// on the submitter\'s side, the protocols that take a buffer, a pending"
770..847 Comment "/// completion or a target\'s pending completion over a session, and one entry"
848..865 Comment "/// of each kind."
